  "repo_truth": "Fresh complete-subject discovery independently passed the exact valid-A/different-valid-B test and validated findings 001/002/003/005, but returned one P2: HCM32-QF-IMPL-DISC-001. In detect_authorized_publication_gap, a later valid matching candidate clears an earlier invalid matching candidate, permitting retry_available for mixed valid+invalid evidence. Stable finding 004 is therefore open and fresh proof claim 006 must be corrected. Exact upstream impact is HIGH: one direct caller, eight upstream symbols, two affected process groups, four modules, entirely inside the already selected Context Resolution recovery/currentness seam.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Use apply_patch to add one focused regression in crates/engine/tests/context_resolution_kernel.rs covering matching valid+invalid eligible recovery candidates in both lexical orders. Establish a genuine RED before production repair; assert fail-closed candidate_invalid/refusal and repository byte stability/idempotence appropriate to the existing recovery contract.",
    "Use apply_patch to make the smallest repair only in detect_authorized_publication_gap in crates/engine/src/context_resolution.rs: invalid/ambiguous evidence matching the authorized outer identity must be monotonic and cannot be cleared by a later valid candidate, while unrelated historical candidates must not poison the current authorized identity.",
    "Do not edit any other production symbol. Preserve one-valid retry, zero candidate, invalid-only, two-valid ambiguity, exact-A quarantine recovery, candidate bounds, currentness, and generic non-HCM behavior.",
    "After focused GREEN, rerun the exact adversarial A/B negative, full Context Resolution kernel, full generic lineage, handbook-engine and workspace all-target/all-feature tests, workspace check, strict Clippy, fmt/diff, ordinary validator, both self-tests, GitNexus scope-all and compare-to-main, base/ref/remote/protected checks.",
    "Update only the fresh proof wall and, only if necessary for truth, the already changed current conditional control docs/SPEC/plan/todo. Record HCM32-QF-IMPL-DISC-001 remediation, RED/GREEN, stable 004 closure, and corrected 006 truth. Do not edit immutable predecessor source evidence."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "Do not modify artifact_lineage_store.rs, artifact_mutation.rs, the original A/B test, fixtures/definitions/profiles, public APIs, dependencies/crates, unsafe/native/platform/transport code, validators/schemas/templates/skills/tooling, handoff records, ledger, or refs.",
    "Do not stage, commit, merge/rebase/reset/clean, create the closure dispatch, push, publish remotely, create HCM-0.11/HCM-3.3 work, or expand beyond the reviewed recovery seam.",
    "Do not treat unrelated historical invalid candidates as current matching corruption and do not weaken fail-closed cardinality or inventory bounds."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Reproduce HCM32-QF-IMPL-DISC-001 with one new test that creates one valid and one invalid eligible candidate claiming the authorized outer identity in each lexical ordering; show the pre-repair classifier yields retry_available or otherwise fails the required candidate_invalid refusal.",
    "Implement the minimal monotonic matching-invalid/ambiguous classification inside detect_authorized_publication_gap only, then run focused GREEN for both orders and existing zero/one/invalid/two-valid classifier tests.",
    "Rerun the complete mandatory proof wall and independently preserve the exact identity-before-mutation A/B test and exact-A recovery behavior.",
    "Correct the fresh proof/control truth, recompute the complete subject manifest, inspect final GitNexus scope for only authorized paths/flows, and return exact commands/counts/timings/hashes plus finding disposition.",
    "Do not declare CLEAN; return remediation complete pending the authorized different-fresh delta closure."
  ],
  "contracts_and_gates": [
    "This is the single consolidated implementation remediation for discovery finding HCM32-QF-IMPL-DISC-001. No unrelated repair or general rediscovery is authorized.",
    "The HIGH impact warning is acknowledged only for the exact previously selected Context Resolution recovery/currentness seam. Any additional HIGH/CRITICAL symbol or path is a stop.",
    "RED/GREEN must cover both lexical orders and distinguish matching invalid evidence from unrelated historical candidates.",
    "All mandatory proof, validator, self-test, GitNexus, remote/base/ref, protected, formatting, and allowlist gates must pass before closure dispatch."
  ],
  "stop_conditions": [
    "Return PROOF_GAP without further code edits on any mandatory post-repair failure; return BLOCKED on another production symbol/path, public/dependency/platform/tooling expansion, or protected/base/ref/remote drift.",
    "Stop if the repair cannot distinguish authorized-identity matching candidates from unrelated history within the existing function and test boundary.",
    "Do not commit or publish; parent owns closure review and P4."
  ],
  "return_contract": {
    "transport": "built_in_subagent",
    "findings_first": true,
